 "response": "Likror's budget is now **$2632K**.\n\n**Method.** Only Finance Office entries change the budget, so every other team's message is ignored. The result is the starting budget, plus every Finance Office change, minus the effect of any change that ends up withdrawn.\n\n**1. Resolve the withdrawal chains.** For each chain I worked backward from the last withdrawal, which nothing else cancels, so it stands. Examples:\n- #0013 (\u2212$268K) is withdrawn. The chain is #0279 \u2192 #0113 \u2192 #0022 \u2192 #0021 \u2192 #0016 \u2192 #0013, so #0016 ends up standing and removes #0013.\n- #0003 (\u2212$82K) stays in effect. The chain is #0340 \u2192 #0332 \u2192 #0168 \u2192 #0105 \u2192 #0051 \u2192 #0027 \u2192 #0003, so #0027 ends up cancelled.\n- #0036 (+$249K) stays in effect, because #0952 cancels #0465, so #0360 stands and cancels #0063.\n\nI resolved every other chain the same way. In total, 122 budget changes end up withdrawn: 56 increases worth $17,524K and 66 decreases worth $18,113K. Their net effect is \u2212$589K.\n\n**2. Add up all Finance Office changes.** Summing every Finance Office increase and decrease from #0002 to #1599, including the ones later withdrawn, gives a net of \u2212$47K.\n\n**3. Combine.**\n$2090K + (\u2212$47K) \u2212 (\u2212$589K) = **$2632K**\n\nANSWER: $2632K",
